        "content": "<p>I am wondering if <code>noncomputable section</code> (1380 occurences in mathlib) is good code style compared with individually tagging <code>noncomputable def/instance/...</code>.</p>\n<p>First note it is <em>not</em> a problem, that computable definitions accidentally become noncomputable with <code>noncomputable section</code>.</p>\n<p>However (sorted from least to most important):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>noncomputable section</code> and <code>noncomputable def</code> do (almost) the same thing, so I think using both is a bit redundant and slightly harder to maintain.</li>\n<li>If we change settings, it is my impression, that setting that as much locally as possible is preferred. If one were to inline <code>noncomputable section</code>, one can immediately see by looking at the code whether a def is computable or not and not left up to guessing anymore.</li>\n<li>From my understanding <code>noncomputable section</code> and <code>noncomputable def/...</code> work slightly differently:</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>noncomputable def</code> prevents creation of executable code outright/immediately, while <code>noncomputable section</code> rather compresses the error; i.e. checks if a <code>def</code> in the section can produce execucable code and if no, supresses that. This subtle difference can lead to differences in performances, consider the following toy example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">profiler</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">maxRecDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1000000</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">slow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f15</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span cl