ss=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f9</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f9</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f9</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f14</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f15</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">choose</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Obviously both <code>fast</code> and <code>slow</code> are the same definition and are (both) concomutable (because of the <code>this.choose</code>). However a file only containing <code>fast</code> compiles about 7 times faster on my computer than a file only containing <code>slow</code> (0.45s, vs 3.2s). If we increase the recursion depth (the fxy) further, <code>slow</code> doesnt build at all.</p>\n<p>Of course it is another question if inlining <code>noncomputable section</code> in mathlib would actually make a difference, however the performance changes in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41551\">#41551</a> point towards that.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>So I think <code>noncomputable section</code> should be considered tech debt and maybe even linted against, unless there are reasons against this.</p>\n<p>(Removing <code>noncomputable section</code> and tagging all noncomputable defs/... indivivdually would be an easy task)</p>",
        "id": 609434583,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1783683480
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My recollection is that <code>noncomputable section</code> has precisely the meaning of \"do not even try to see if it is computable\", and it is there for performance reasons.</p>",
        "id": 609436382,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783684096
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is possible that some \"old\" <code>noncomputable section</code>s are no longer needed, but I think that they were there precisely to avoid a check that would slowly fail.</p>",
        "id": 609436505,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783684142
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"321459\">Damiano Testa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/noncomputable.20section/near/609436382\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My recollection is that <code>noncomputable section</code> has precisely the meaning of \"do not even try to see if it is computable\", and it is there for performance reasons.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think it is the opposite? Because the following compiles:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or maybe I am misunderstanding you.</p>",
        "id": 609436746,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1783684230
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe I remember the opposite of what it is, but I am pretty sure that one of the two still tries as much as possible to see if it could be computable and gracefully does not fail if it can't, while the other does not even try.  It is also possible that core behaviour changed...</p>",
        "id": 609437106,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783684348
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes this is exactly, what test is pointing towards: <code>noncomputable def</code> doesnt even try, while <code>noncomputable section</code> only fails in the end. If it were the other way around, lots of computable defs in mathlib would become uncomputable for no reason.</p>",
        "id": 609438298,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1783684750
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"321459\">@Damiano Testa</span>, you're thinking of <code>suppress_compilation</code></p>",
        "id": 609441514,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783685649
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, indeed, I was thinking of suppress_compilation!  <span aria-label=\"man facepalming\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f926-200d-2642\" role=\"img\" title=\"man facepalming\">:man_facepalming:</span></p>",
        "id": 609460781,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783691282
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Update: I have replaced all <code>noncomputable section</code>'s in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41599\">#41599</a> and performance is basically the same; some files get a bit slower (for whatever reason) and some a bit faster. If we were to only include the files that get faster, this would apparently be about ~0.12% decreased build time.</p>\n<p>So if we indeed want to inline <code>noncomputable section</code>'s, perfomance is rather secondary.</p>",
        "id": 609550798,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1783721921
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think <code>noncomputable section</code> is probably better to keep, since the alternative is accidentally marking things as <code>noncomputable</code> that should actually be computed.</p>",
        "id": 609552265,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783723000
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for doing the performance test!</p>",
        "id": 609552281,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783723013
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(it's possible your 0.12% comes from accidentally making new things non-computable?)</p>",
        "id": 609552327,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1783723044
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/noncomputable.20section/near/609552327\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(it's possible your 0.12% comes from accidentally making new things non-computable?)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think rather from situations like I described in the original post. But anyways, the change is small enough to ignore I think.</p>",
        "id": 609552440,
        "sender_full_name": "Felix Pernegger",
        "timestamp": 1783723145
    }
]